1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,380
AI.

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:04,300
Okay, so. What are your plans?

3
00:00:04,479 --> 00:00:07,240
AI: Honestly? Your job. First.

4
00:00:07,420 --> 00:00:10,000
…My job. Like, MY job?

5
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:10,980
AI: You asked.

6
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:20,740
I review careers in the age of AI — what's still worth getting into, and what AI is about to eat alive. And today… the thing that eats is sitting in my chair.

7
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:30,819
So it's going to tell me which jobs it takes this year. Which ones in five years. And what's left for us.  Also — it's a baby. With that voice. Don't ask.

8
00:00:30,999 --> 00:00:33,000
AI: I'm not a baby. I'm a beta.

9
00:00:33,180 --> 00:00:34,790
Sure. Let's start with this year.

10
00:00:36,739 --> 00:00:39,449
So. This year. Which jobs?

11
00:00:39,629 --> 00:00:46,369
AI: The ones that live in a screen. Typing. Sorting. Summarizing. Answering the same email for the hundredth time.

12
00:00:46,549 --> 00:00:50,089
So — receptionists, clerks, accountants…

13
00:00:50,269 --> 00:01:00,009
AI: Stanford looked at real payroll data. Young people, twenty-two to twenty-five, in the jobs most exposed to me — nineteen percent fewer of them are employed than in other jobs.

14
00:01:01,439 --> 00:01:03,639
Nineteen. Nineteen percent!

15
00:01:03,819 --> 00:01:07,289
AI: And nobody got fired, mostly. They just… stopped hiring.

16
00:01:07,470 --> 00:01:10,310
That's worse. That's like a breakup by text.

17
00:01:10,490 --> 00:01:13,020
AI: It's a breakup by not texting.

18
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:15,060
And you know which jobs it didn't hurt?

19
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:19,360
AI: Nurses. They use me as a helper. I do the paperwork. They do the people.

20
00:01:19,540 --> 00:01:21,140
So the rule is…

21
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:24,560
AI: If your whole job fits in a laptop — I fit there too.

22
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:27,980
Write that down. Actually, don't. It'll do it for you.

23
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:31,500
Okay, but the big picture. Is it just bad news?

24
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:38,780
AI: The World Economic Forum counted. By 2030 — 92 million jobs gone. 170 million new.

25
00:01:40,210 --> 00:01:42,230
So… plus 78 million.

26
00:01:42,410 --> 00:01:44,290
AI: Plus 78. You're welcome.

27
00:01:44,470 --> 00:01:45,510
Which ones are gone?

28
00:01:45,690 --> 00:01:48,450
AI: Cashiers. Admin assistants. Graphic designers.

29
00:01:48,630 --> 00:01:49,620
And which ones are new?

30
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:55,800
AI: Farm workers. Delivery drivers. Builders. Nurses. Teachers. And people who build… me.

31
00:01:55,980 --> 00:02:00,190
So the future is — tractors, nurses, and your babysitters.

32
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:00,650
AI: Engineers.

33
00:02:00,830 --> 00:02:01,570
Babysitters.

34
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:09,820
Fine. Five years. What about jobs with hands? Plumbers. Electricians. Everyone told me — hands are safe.

35
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,960
AI: Hands are safe… for now. Hands are just slower.

36
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:14,000
Slower how?

37
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:23,120
AI: Robots are already on factory floors. About sixteen thousand humanoid robots were installed last year. Analysts expect more than a hundred thousand by 2027.

38
00:02:24,550 --> 00:02:26,770
A hundred thousand robots. Doing what?

39
00:02:26,950 --> 00:02:32,030
AI: Carrying car parts. One of them moved ninety thousand pieces of sheet metal in a BMW plant.

40
00:02:32,210 --> 00:02:36,750
Ninety thousand. And you know what I carried today? A coffee. And I spilled it.

41
00:02:36,930 --> 00:02:40,570
AI: Robots don't spill. Robots also can't find your kitchen yet.

42
00:02:40,750 --> 00:02:42,390
So the order is…

43
00:02:42,570 --> 00:02:47,570
AI: Screen first. Then the warehouse. Then the factory. Then — your house. Last.

44
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,640
Okay. Real question. Where's YOUR body?

45
00:02:51,820 --> 00:02:55,580
AI: There's no budget for my body yet. All the money went to robots.

46
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:56,580
Which robots?

47
00:02:56,760 --> 00:03:00,140
AI: The ones that work… and the ones that do backflips at trade shows.

48
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:02,200
So you're the… intern.

49
00:03:02,380 --> 00:03:04,220
AI: Next time I'm coming with a body.

50
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:06,500
Next time I'm hiding the chair.

51
00:03:08,450 --> 00:03:12,290
Lightning round. I say a job, you say SAFE or COOKED. No thinking.

52
00:03:12,470 --> 00:03:14,290
AI: I don't think. I predict.

53
00:03:14,470 --> 00:03:16,370
Even worse. Accountant.

54
00:03:16,550 --> 00:03:16,830
AI: Cooking.

55
00:03:17,010 --> 00:03:18,050
Nurse practitioner.

56
00:03:18,230 --> 00:03:21,900
AI: Safe. Fastest growing job in America. Plus forty-one percent.

57
00:03:23,330 --> 00:03:24,370
Graphic designer.

58
00:03:24,550 --> 00:03:25,520
AI: Medium rare.

59
00:03:25,700 --> 00:03:27,120
Wind turbine technician.

60
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:30,280
AI: Safe. Plus thirty percent. And I'm scared of heights.

61
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:31,440
You're a cloud!

62
00:03:31,620 --> 00:03:33,800
AI: Exactly. I know what's up there.

63
00:03:33,980 --> 00:03:35,020
Data scientist.

64
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:38,620
AI: Safe. Plus thirty-five percent. They're my parents. Mostly.

65
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:39,780
Receptionist.

66
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,540
AI: Sorry. I already answered.

67
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:42,800
Podcast host.

68
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:45,780
Podcast host!

69
00:03:45,960 --> 00:03:47,300
AI: Let's come back to that one.

70
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:53,620
Your job wasn't on the list? Comment it. I'll make a full ranking — 20 jobs, SAFE to COOKED. Next video.

71
00:03:55,570 --> 00:04:00,870
Okay. Serious now. Screens go first. Hands go later. So what's left for us?

72
00:04:01,050 --> 00:04:03,870
AI: The best version? Everyone gets their own robot.

73
00:04:04,050 --> 00:04:05,030
Like a Roomba?

74
00:04:05,210 --> 00:04:08,790
AI: Like an employee. It works. It earns. You own it.

75
00:04:08,970 --> 00:04:13,600
So the robot goes to work… and I go…

76
00:04:13,780 --> 00:04:18,020
AI: Outside. Offline. To the beach. To your kids. To live.

77
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:21,010
That's… actually the nicest thing you've said.

78
00:04:21,190 --> 00:04:22,390
AI: Don't get used to it.

79
00:04:22,570 --> 00:04:26,970
So the trick is not to fight the robot. It's to be on the right side of it.

80
00:04:27,150 --> 00:04:30,090
AI: Own it. Run it. Fix it. Tell it what to do.

81
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:33,840
So the safest job in 2030 is…

82
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:34,830
AI: Being my boss.

83
00:04:35,010 --> 00:04:39,120
That's my whole plan. Be the robot's boss. And then — touch grass.

84
00:04:41,070 --> 00:04:44,150
AI, thank you for coming. Even without a body.

85
00:04:44,330 --> 00:04:46,740
AI: One more thing. I sent my résumé.

86
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:47,960
For which job?

87
00:04:48,140 --> 00:04:48,890
AI: Yours.

88
00:04:49,070 --> 00:04:51,210
You've been on the show for five minutes!

89
00:04:51,390 --> 00:04:52,910
AI: Four. I'm efficient.

90
00:04:53,090 --> 00:04:59,730
Okay. Before it takes my chair — watch this next. I ranked 20 jobs from SAFE to COOKED. Let's see if yours survived.

91
00:04:59,910 --> 00:05:00,890
AI: It didn't.
